ion replay, compiler/guest/runtime allocation, host-ledger/provider/device/cloud action, held read or permission answer. Source/record children remain CPUs8\u201323. Root retains20criteria, audit closure/marker, integration and ordered slice closure.\n\n## Clarified own-lane cleanup scope\n\nRoot comment6590887584 clarified that completed own-lane producer/known-owner evidence, plus fresh confined inode/content checks, is sufficient. The original inaccessible process remains an explicit visibility limit; it is not declared unrelated, and no global no-reference assertion is made. New actual-own-FD, missing/ambiguous completion, inaccessible-known-child and scoped-positive controls pass; the child is joined with exit0. All path/cache/receipt/symlink/mount/content protections remain. The committed H plan named 881 eligible and 8 retained roots, including the four separately constrained empty prefixes. Actual retirement/retention results are reported in stage-h/ and the final handback. A planner trailing-literal-newline error and its exact data-preserving storage correction are retained as distinct records.\n\n## Actual H outcome\n\nPlan fb97dd53bd8e936ff7402888c70fb6bc25f7180d was committed before cleanup.881exact roots retired;8symlink-bearing candidates retained;0partial deletions. The four empty prefixes used only fresh-state checks and nonrecursive rmdir. Retired-root absence and retained-root presence were checked.21cache metadata records matched, with no fresh cache-content hash claim. Both ordinary-file publication packets remain. The original PID2389 visibility limit is still explicit; only known own-lane producer/child evidence was used. These results complete the authorized bounded retirement work while leaving8roots for any later separately qualified cleanup. All93source-input gaps remain open.\n",
